        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6a4694cc-ecfa-5c72-9726-bf6c2691bb06",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Definitions of Canadian serial killers\n- People: Keith Hunter Jesperson, Gordon Stewart Northcott, William Dean Christenson, Earle Nelson, Earle Leonard Nelson\n\nFacts:\n- The book \"Cold North Killer's\" defines a Canadian serial killer to include Canadians who committed murder abroad.\n- The book \"Cold North Killer's\" defines a Canadian serial killer to include non-Canadians who committed murder in Canada.\n- Keith Hunter Jesperson and Gordon Stewart Northcott are examples in \"Cold North Killer's\" of Canadians who committed murder abroad.\n- William Dean Christenson and Earle Nelson are examples in \"Cold North Killer's\" of non-Canadians who committed murder in Canada.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson, known as \"the Gorilla Man,\" was born on May 12, 1897.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson was an American serial killer.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson died on January 13, 1928.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
